## Hints for Future Agents
Chat still rejects oversized names before the strict check, so the truncation only ever shows on the Responses path (and for dynamic Kimi tools, which also go through validate_tools after normalization). The exact-message assertions elsewhere use short names and are unaffected. The HTTP acceptance test still covers omitted strict, strict false, strict true with a valid schema, and strict true with omitted parameters.

## Codebase Discoveries
MAX_FUNCTION_NAME_LENGTH is pub in validate.rs and is a byte length there; bounded_name counts chars so a multi-byte name is never split mid-character.

